        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          This table gives bone histomorphometric parameters in response to three different doses of vitamin E in rats that were either hindlimb-unloaded or ambulatory.  Bone volume normalized to tissue volume (BV/TV) is given in percent, as is bone surface normalized to tissue volume (BS/TV).  Characteristics of the bone trabeculae, a supporting bone network of spicules, are given in trabecular thickness (TbTh), trabecular separation (TbSp), and trabecular number (TbN).  These parameters give insight on bone density and strength.    The trabeculae of healthy bone have a higher number, are thicker, and are better connected.   The mineral apposition rate (MAR) is given in micrometers per day, and the bone formation rate normalized to bone volume is given in percent per day.  <P>As reported in: Smith BJ, Lucas EA, Turner RT, Evans GL, Lerner MR, Brackett DJ, Stoecker BJ, Arjmandi BH. Vitamin E provides protection for bone in mature hindlimb unloaded male rats. <I>Calcified Tissue International.</I> 2004 Mar.
        </div>

